│ patch_name               │ heap_packing                                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the inner linear scan over all packs with a min-heap. The original constrained    │
│                          │ LPT packing repeatedly finds the least-loaded non-full pack in O(num_packs), making       │
│                          │ packing expensive when there are many GPUs/nodes. A heap preserves the same greedy policy │
│                          │ while reducing this selection to O(log(num_packs)). Converting the already CPU-resident   │
│                          │ per-layer weights and sorted indices to Python lists also avoids repeated scalar Tensor   │
│                          │ operations and tensor-to-Python comparisons inside the hot loop.                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is especially beneficial because balanced_packing is called for both node placement  │
│                          │ and GPU placement across every MoE layer. The resulting assignment remains the same       │
│                          │ greedy largest-first load balancing strategy, including the exact cardinality constraint  │
│                          │ per pack.                                                                                 │
