│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ heap_packing                                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the inner constrained-LPT packing loop with a heap-based implementation.          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The existing implementation scans every non-full pack for every group and performs Python │
│                          │ comparisons/additions on scalar tensors. This is costly, especially during the            │
│                          │ physical-expert-to-GPU packing stage where there can be many physical experts. A min-heap │
│                          │ selects the least-loaded available pack in O(log(num_packs)) while preserving the same    │
│                          │ largest-weight-first greedy policy and exact per-pack cardinality constraint.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Weights and sorted indices are converted to Python values once per call, avoiding         │
│                          │ repeated CPU scalar tensor operations. This reduces rearrangement latency without         │
│                          │ changing the placement policy's balancing objective.                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
