│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ packing_swap_refinement                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Add a bounded local-search refinement after largest-processing-time packing. The existing │
│                          │ heap policy is fast, but it can become trapped when equal-cardinality packs contain a     │
│                          │ heavy item paired with a medium item while a lighter pack has a compensating item. A swap │
│                          │ preserves the mandatory number of experts/groups per pack and can reduce the maximum      │
│                          │ GPU/node load without changing replica counts or mappings.                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The refinement evaluates swaps only between the currently most-loaded pack and            │
│                          │ less-loaded packs, chooses the best max-load reduction, and caps work to two improving    │
│                          │ swaps per layer. This keeps the additional CPU cost small while directly optimizing the   │
│                          │ bottleneck load that determines expert-parallel execution time.                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0408                                                                                   │
