│ patch_name               │ heap_refined_eplb                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ This version retains the fast heap-based largest-processing-time packing policy from the  │
│                          │ faster prior implementation, while adding a small bounded local-swap refinement pass. The │
│                          │ refinement preserves the exact equal-cardinality constraint for every pack and only       │
│                          │ accepts swaps that strictly reduce the current maximum pack load.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Implementation improvements include:                                                      │
│                          │ - Heap-based least-loaded-pack selection rather than scanning all packs.                  │
│                          │ - Python-list construction for packing rows, avoiding repeated scalar Torch writes in hot │
│                          │ loops.                                                                                    │
│                          │ - Bounded local refinement to improve GPU/node load balance beyond greedy LPT placement.  │
│                          │ - Reused inverse-permutation helper and more direct tensor construction.                  │
│                          │ - Preserved public API, output shapes, dtypes, and mapping semantics.                     │
