│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ heavy_partner_swap                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Improve the cardinality-preserving packing refinement without returning to the expensive  │
│                          │ exhaustive all-pack-pair search. The current refinement only exchanges an item between    │
│                          │ the heaviest and lightest packs. That misses valid improvements where moving an item to   │
│                          │ the lightest pack would make it the new bottleneck, while exchanging with a moderately    │
│                          │ loaded pack reduces the global maximum.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This change evaluates swaps from the current bottleneck pack with every other pack. It    │
│                          │ retains the low complexity of a targeted local search, preserves exact per-GPU capacity,  │
│                          │ and directly optimizes the maximum GPU load. It should improve GPU balancedness on skewed │
│                          │ distributions while adding only a small bounded amount of work per packing row.           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
