│ patch_name               │ swap_refined_packing                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Improve the capacity-constrained LPT packing heuristic with a bounded local-search        │
│                          │ refinement phase.                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The existing heap-based assignment is fast, but greedy choices can leave a heavy          │
│                          │ expert/group paired with smaller items on an overloaded GPU or node while a beneficial    │
│                          │ swap exists elsewhere. This is particularly relevant after replication, where             │
│                          │ physical-expert loads are often skewed and GPU balancedness is a major component of the   │
│                          │ score.                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ After the initial assignment, this edit repeatedly examines swaps between an item in a    │
│                          │ most-loaded pack and an item in another pack. It accepts the swap that lexicographically  │
│                          │ improves (1) maximum pack load and then (2) total squared pack load. The latter permits   │
│                          │ useful equal-makespan rearrangements that can unlock a later maximum-load reduction. The  │
│                          │ number of accepted swaps is bounded by `num_packs`, preserving predictable and low        │
│                          │ overhead while materially improving local packing quality. Cardinality constraints remain │
│                          │ exactly satisfied because every operation is a swap.                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
