│ patch_name               │ waterfill_lpt_rebalance                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces iterative replica selection with a vectorized discrete       │
│                          │ water-filling formulation: every possible additional replica contributes a marginal load  │
│                          │ value `weight / replica_rank`, and selecting the globally largest marginal values         │
│                          │ produces the minimax-optimal replica counts for the fixed replica budget.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Physical replicas are then placed with capacity-constrained LPT scheduling, followed by a │
│                          │ bounded best-improving cross-GPU swap pass. This jointly improves per-expert replica      │
│                          │ balance and GPU load balance while avoiding the repeated per-replica `max(weight /        │
│                          │ count)` loop used previously. Group-to-node placement retains hierarchical locality when  │
│                          │ possible.                                                                                 │
