│ patch_name               │ scalar_free_packing_and_replication                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ `balanced_packing` performs its greedy assignment in Python, but its current inner loop   │
│                          │ repeatedly indexes PyTorch scalar tensors and accumulates scalar tensors in a Python      │
│                          │ list. This creates substantial dispatcher and scalar-object overhead for every group      │
│                          │ assignment. Convert each sorted row and its weights to Python lists once, so the greedy   │
│                          │ LPT-with-capacity policy operates on native Python integers/floats while preserving the   │
│                          │ same ordering and assignment rule.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ `replicate_experts` also allocates a fresh division result for every redundant replica.   │
│                          │ Reuse a preallocated floating-point score buffer with `torch.div(..., out=...)`. Replica  │
│                          │ selections remain strictly sequential, so the existing `argmax(weight / logcnt)` greedy   │
│                          │ behavior is unchanged after every count update.                                           │
