│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ waterline_slot_packing                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ This version replaces the layer-by-layer Python greedy loops with two batched tensor      │
│                          │ algorithms.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For replication, it uses an exact discrete waterline formulation: the value of assigning  │
│                          │ an expert its k-th replica is `load / k`. Selecting the globally largest redundant        │
│                          │ replica waterlines per layer minimizes the largest per-replica logical-expert load under  │
│                          │ the fixed replica budget. This computes all replica counts with one batched `topk`,       │
│                          │ rather than repeatedly running a maximum reduction once per redundant expert.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For node and GPU placement, it uses batched antitone slot packing. Experts are sorted by  │
│                          │ load, then processed in pack-sized rounds. In every round, the currently heaviest items   │
│                          │ are paired with the currently lightest packs, while preserving the exact number of        │
│                          │ experts assigned to every pack. This is a vectorized largest-processing-time-style        │
│                          │ balancing heuristic, avoids per-layer Python work, and directly respects fixed GPU        │
│                          │ capacity.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The hierarchy and output contract remain unchanged: group locality is retained whenever   │
│                          │ groups divide nodes, while the fallback remains global balancing.                         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
