│ patch_description        │ This implementation keeps the hierarchical topology-aware structure, but replaces the     │
│                          │ purely one-pass group packing behavior with a bounded local-refinement strategy.          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The initial placement still uses fast largest-first heap scheduling, which provides a     │
│                          │ strong starting solution efficiently. After this placement, a small number of             │
│                          │ deterministic exchanges between the currently heaviest and lightest packs is evaluated.   │
│                          │ An exchange is accepted only when it strictly improves the global load-range objective    │
│                          │ (with squared load deviation as a tie-breaker). This preserves exact per-pack capacity    │
│                          │ while improving GPU and node balance in cases where greedy placement becomes trapped in a │
│                          │ locally suboptimal arrangement.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It also adds safe fast paths for one-pack, one-item-per-pack, and exactly uniform         │
│                          │ weights. These cases need no sorting, heap operations, or refinement and directly         │
│                          │ construct a stable contiguous mapping.                                                    │
